Third-party origins
===================

src/core/e2sysex.ts, src/core/hacktribeNrpn.ts, src/core/e2FxParams.ts,
src/core/hacktribeRam.ts
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The KORG Electribe 2 SysEx protocol implementation and the KORG 8-bit <-> 7-bit
codec are ported from:

    hacktribe / hacktribe-editor
    Copyright (C) bangcorrupt
    https://github.com/bangcorrupt/hacktribe
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

Specifically, the message framing (F0 42 3g 00 01 <id> <msgId> ... F7), the
message-ID table, the acknowledgement codes (ht_sysex_format) and the pattern
dump/write byte order (e2pat2syx.py) follow that implementation.

The NRPN layer (hacktribeNrpn.ts) follows utils/ht_nrpn_format.py and the
hacktribe wiki MIDI.md; the FX type and parameter tables (e2FxParams.ts) follow
utils/ht_fx_ram_format.py and utils/ht_fx_preset_format.py. Both were taken via
Synthstudio, which ported them from the same source. The RAM peek/poke layer
(hacktribeRam.ts) follows utils/ht_sysex.py; its address map is documented in
omnitribe/docs/reverse/hacktribe_ram_and_formats.md.

TekkForge is therefore distributed under the GPL-3.0-or-later as well.


E2S / ESX-1 file-format knowledge
---------------------------------
The `.all` sample-bank layout (offset table at 0x0010, 1020 LE32 entries) and
the korg/esli sub-chunk field offsets were verified against:

    Oe2sSLE — Open e2sSample.all Editor
    Copyright (C) Jonathan Taquet
    https://github.com/JonathanTaquet/Oe2sSLE
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2.0 or later

No Oe2sSLE code is included; only the on-disk structure documented by that
project was used, cross-checked against real device banks.


